<title>USA: U.S. Oct retail sales rose 0.2 percent.</title>
<headline>U.S. Oct retail sales rose 0.2 percent.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commerce Department seasonally adjusted data on U.S. retail sales.</p>
<p>    Percent Changes:   Oct     Sept--Rev from     Oct96/95</p>
<p> Retail Sales	    0.2	0.8     0.7	   5.2</p>
<p> Excluding Autos	 0.4	0.5     0.4	   4.8</p>
<p> Auto Sales	     -0.3	1.7     1.7	   6.5</p>
<p> Durable Goods	  UNCH	0.9     0.9	   6.5</p>
<p> NonDurable Goods	0.3	0.7     0.6	   4.4</p>
<p> Furniture Stores     -1.0     -0.2    -0.3	   2.7</p>
<p> Building Materials    0.7	0.4     0.1	   7.7</p>
<p>    Billions of Dlrs: Oct	Sept--Rev from    Aug--Rev from</p>
<p> Retail Sales	 206.58   206.20   205.71   204.60   204.25</p>
<p> Excluding Autos    155.85   155.31   154.90   154.58   154.28</p>
<p> Auto Sales	    50.73    50.89    50.81    50.02    49.98</p>
<p> Durable Goods	 84.27    84.30    84.18    83.54    83.47</p>
<p> NonDurable Goods   122.31   121.90   121.53   121.06   120.78</p>
<p> Furniture Stores    11.37    11.49    11.48    11.51    11.52</p>
<p> Building Materials  11.28    11.20    11.14    11.16    11.13</p>
<p>    Percent Changes:   Oct     Sept--Rev from    Oct96/95</p>
<p> General Merchandise   0.7     UNCH     0.3	   6.2</p>
<p> Department Stores     0.4	0.3     0.5	   6.1</p>
<p> Food Stores	     0.7	1.1     1.2	   4.1</p>
<p> Grocery Stores	  0.8	1.2     1.2	   4.3</p>
<p> Gas Stations	    0.1	0.4     0.6	   7.1</p>
<p> Apparel Stores	 -0.3	1.0    -0.1	   4.7</p>
<p> Eat/Drink Places     -0.1	0.6     0.5	   1.0</p>
<p> Drug Stores	     1.0	0.1    -0.3	   6.9</p>
<p>    Billions of Dlrs: Oct	Sept--Rev from     Aug--Rev from</p>
<p> General Merch.	26.11    25.93    26.02     25.92   25.95</p>
<p> Department Stores   20.32    20.24    20.28     20.17   20.17</p>
<p> Food Stores	   35.89    35.64    35.65     35.25   35.24</p>
<p> Grocery Stores	34.07    33.80    33.78     33.38   33.38</p>
<p> Gas Stations	  13.02    13.01    12.95     12.96   12.87</p>
<p> Apparel Stores	 9.48     9.51     9.36	9.42    9.37</p>
<p> Eat/Drink Places    19.81    19.82    19.65     19.70   19.54</p>
<p> Drug Stores	    7.58     7.51     7.49	7.50 p 7n</p>
<p>Wall Street ecoonomists expected October retail sales to rise 0.3 percent, and sales excluding autos to be up 0.3 percent.  </p>
<p>The department revised August retail sales to a 0.1 percent fall from a 0.2 percent drop. It revised August sales excluding autos to off 0.3 percent from a 0.5 percent decrease, and August auto sales to a 0.6 percent increase from up 0.5 percent.</p>
